o Targeted bloom filters on equality-key columns. buildParquetCopySQL()'s option
  list (FORMAT / COMPRESSION / COMPRESSION_LEVEL / ROW_GROUP_SIZE / PARTITION_BY
  / APPEND in R/parquet-io.R) has no WRITE_BLOOM_FILTER; coverage is currently
  path-dependent: DuckDB COPY paths write blooms on ALL columns (footer bloat),
  while the arrow paths (write_parquet / write_dataset) write NONE. Add a
  bloom_columns argument defaulting to the integer key spine (indexcol,
  __sample__, __feature__, from, to) that emits WRITE_BLOOM_FILTER on the COPY
  paths and the equivalent arrow option, for uniform, targeted coverage instead
  of all-or-nothing. Faithful (footer metadata only). Bounded value: blooms help
  rare-value equality lookups substantially but do nothing for common values, so
  this is hygiene/consistency, not a headline win.

o Export a documented low-level space-filling-curve ordering API (Morton N-D /
  Hilbert 2-D / lexicographic; currently zorder() / hilbert() / the internal
  .clusterOrderSQL) and .columnExtents(), so that DuckDBArray's COO writer (see
  DuckDBArray/TODO) and any downstream serving-layer builder reuse ONE curve
  implementation rather than re-deriving it. The codebase already treats "single
  Morton implementation" as a tenet (DuckDBSpatial R/points-coord-index.R); this
  promotes it to a stable API.
